<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s349S">&quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w5">What</span>,&quot; one may ask, &quot;is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w4">basic nature</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w3">each</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w2">ten</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w1">non-<span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s349m1">virtues</span></span>?&quot; The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w6">taking of <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s349m2">life</span></span> is defined as <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w10">killing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w9">another</span> being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w7">purposely</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s349p1">without</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w8">mistake</span>. The word &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w11">purposely</span>&quot; is meant to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w16">indicate</span> that there is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w15">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w14">problem</span> like where the being in question has <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w13">died</span> but there was <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s349p2">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s349w12">intent</span>.</span>
</div>
